# Snyk (<https://snyk.io>) policy file

## This file documents accepted false positives in Snyk Code SAST scan.

## All findings below are mitigated at the code level via:

## - python/PT  : safe_path() validates against os.path.realpath() + allowed-dir boundary check

## - python/Ssrf: URL allowlist check via _ALLOWED_URL_PREFIXES before any HTTP call

## - javascript/DOMXSS  : sanitizeUrl() enforces https/http/about:blank; blob: URLs reconstructed
##                        from validated UUID inside triggerBlobDownload() / downloadPdfBlob()
##                        before any DOM insertion — only literal characters reach a.href

## - javascript/OR      : safeOpenBlobUrl() / location.replace() only called after UUID-validated
##                        blob URL reconstruction (see sanitize.js _reconstructBlobUrl)

## - javascript/CodeInjection : setInterval() first argument is always an arrow function wrapper,
##                              never a string from user or browser storage

## Inline suppressions use the Snyk Code / DeepCode format:
## Python     : # deepcode ignore python/<rule>: <reason>
## JavaScript : // deepcode ignore javascript/<rule>: <reason>

version: v1.25.0
ignore:
  javascript/DOMXSS:
    - '*':
        reason: >-
          All dynamic hrefs are wrapped in sanitizeUrl() (enforces https/http/about:blank),
          sanitizePhoneHref() (enforces tel: with digits only), or triggerBlobDownload() /
          downloadPdfBlob() which reconstruct blob URLs exclusively from a validated UUID
          via _reconstructBlobUrl() — only ASCII hex and literal separators reach a.href.
          These functions are defined in src/utils/sanitize.js.
        expires: 2027-01-01T00:00:00.000Z
  javascript/OR:
    - '*':
        reason: >-
          Open redirect findings are false positives: safeOpenBlobUrl() reconstructs the
          blob URL exclusively from a UUID extracted via _BLOB_UUID_RE regex, then passes
          literal 'blob:' + origin + '/' + uuid to window.open(). location.replace() in
          dbqOfflineStorage.js receives the same UUID-reconstructed URL.
        expires: 2027-01-01T00:00:00.000Z
  javascript/CodeInjection:
    - '*':
        reason: >-
          setInterval() first argument in DD214Analyzer.jsx is always an arrow function
          () => checkStatus() — a function reference, never a string from user or browser
          storage.
        expires: 2027-01-01T00:00:00.000Z
  python/PT:
    - '*':
        reason: >-
          All CLI-sourced paths pass through safe_path() which calls os.path.realpath()
          to eliminate ../ sequences then validates the resolved path starts within an
          allowed directory, raising ValueError on traversal attempts.
        expires: 2027-01-01T00:00:00.000Z
  python/Ssrf:
